  "id": "spinal-reflex",
  "term": "spinal reflex",
  "definition": "A spinal reflex is a response produced through spinal cord pathways, here described as being evoked in lower-limb muscles by stimulation that activates sensory fibers. In this context, it can be measured across several muscles by examining the size and recruitment of the muscle responses.",
